I wrote a little program to show the RECORD file in the same format as
the game itself uses at the end and with the -s option. I included the
options -u and -<character> from the game itself, and -d to display
the game ending dates and -n to display a given number of scores.
And there is -f to read another file of the same format, like the logfile.
I wrote it partially to practice the C language, with no previous
knowledge of the language.. it's writtten for MSDOS with Borland C,
but I believe it is quite portable to other compilers and operating 
systems. A part of the comments and variable names are in Finnish,
I didn't bother translating everything, but the output is English.
If you find any bugs or have some way of death that this program shows
with the text "killed by" and the game itself says something else 
(I don't have the source, I just inspected my RECORD and LOGFILE),
please tell me by mail.
Here you go:

